 ## Background
-Splatapult was created by Anthony J. Thibault and released as an open-source program to display 3D Gaussian Splatting files (PLY). It is based on the implementation of Intel's Embree radix sort, adapted for Vulkan/OpenGL compute shaders. The project includes build scripts for CMake and vcpkg, and supports various rendering options like sRGB and full SH [S1, unofficial]. It is used in Android, Apple, Web, Flutter, and React Native SDKs for real-time on-device Gaussian Splatting rendering [S2, unofficial].
